{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"4043256d8ce6767d09a8896b7cfac7be1fd34f002eccdb48cb1186fec9ec38fa","digest":{"component_or_area":"grounding metric backend (Engine B)","key_entities":["src/rebar/grounding/engine_b_backends.py::_metric_invoke","src/rebar/grounding/engine_b_backends.py::_scc_files","rebar.builtin.smell.metric-oversize","scc --by-file --format json","Files array","Code field","tests/unit/grounding/test_engine_b.py::test_metric_backend_requests_per_file_json_and_emits_only_over_cutoff"],"problem_keywords":["scc","per-file entries","metric detection","LOC threshold","grounding backend"],"propositions":["_metric_invoke invokes scc without --by-file, causing scc 3.7.0 to return language summaries with empty Files arrays instead of per-file entries","_scc_files depends on per-file entries in the Files array but receives none, preventing the threshold loop from executing and emitting no metric matches","The metric-oversize detector promises per-file matches for files exceeding 800 LOC but cannot emit any because _metric_invoke prevents scc from returning per-file data","The fix adds --by-file to the scc invocation in _metric_invoke, enabling _scc_files to parse per-file entries and correctly emit matches for files above the LOC cutoff","Existing fail-open semantics for tool absence, timeouts, nonzero exit, and invalid JSON remain unchanged by the fix"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787313765051291001,"uuid":"00e7ad24-b65b-415a-aefc-23177fca4005"}